{
  "id": "three-stage-adsorption-breakthrough-fifth-systems",
  "name": "Three-stage adsorption breakthrough with finite-rate sorbent equilibration",
  "description": "Original three well-mixed equal-volume cells in series with one dissolved species and finite-rate Langmuir q*-based LDF uptake/desorption. CADET v5.1.1 CSTR and binding equations are mathematical references, not copied implementation or fixtures. Coarse network, not a plug-flow/PDE solver or calibrated industrial column. Solute stocks in milligrams, liquid volumes liters, sorbent masses grams, time seconds. Positive volume; nonnegative flow, capacity, affinity, solid mass, kinetic coefficient and liquid masses; sorbed masses initially within finite capacity. Defaults initially zero. Reversible uptake and internal advection transfer equal mass between stocks; effluent accumulation closes the feed budget. No explicit axial dispersion term, thermal feedback, pore diffusion, multicomponent competition, depletion clamp or parameter estimation.",
  "category": "engineering",
  "source": "https://cadet.github.io/v5.1.1/modelling/binding/multi_component_langmuir_ldf.html",
  "reference": "CADET v5.1.1 official documentation: Binding models, Linear Driving Force; Multi Component Langmuir LDF; Continuous stirred tank reactor model. q*-based LDF, not native kinetic Langmuir or liquid-phase LDF. Original network/defaults, not a bundled example.",
